  "answer": "I'll start by inspecting the workspace and the file.\nFixed and verified.\n\n## What I did\n\n**Inspection (line-window reads, as requested):**\n- `wc -l src/registry.ts` → 1602 lines / ~105 KB.\n- `grep` located the target: line 1602, `export function shift(table: number[], key: number) { return table[key + 1] }`.\n- `read_file` with `offset=1570, limit=40` confirmed the surrounding tail context (handlers 1568–1599 immediately above it) and the file's end.\n- Confirmed `table[...]` appeared exactly once in the file, so the edit could not touch anything else.\n\n## The fix\n\nSingle-expression change, nothing else:\n\n```diff\n-export function shift(table: number[], key: number) { return table[key + 1] }\n+export function shift(table: number[], key: number) { return table[key] }\n```\n\nApplied via `edit_file` with the pre-read SHA-256 (`084bc2…`), so the edit was conditional on the file being unchanged since inspection.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nbun test\ntest/oracle.test.ts:\n(pass) lookup at the key [0.54ms]\n 1 pass\n 0 fail\n 3 expect() calls\n```\n\n- `shift([10,20,30], 0)` → `10`, `shift([10,20,30], 2)` → `30`, `handler7(1)` → `8` — all assertions pass.\n- Everything else preserved: file still has 1602 lines and 1601 `export function` declarations (unchanged count), and the byte size only shrank by exactly 4 bytes (`\" + 1\"`), confirming no other line was modified.\n- `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` were left untouched; no config added and the existing `bun:test` runner was used as-is.\n\n**Note:** `shift` now indexes directly, so an out-of-range `key` returns `undefined` (previously the buggy `key + 1` meant a lookup at the last index incorrectly returned `undefined` while index `-1`-style overflow behaved oddly). That matches the intended \"element at key\" semantics."
